<h2 class="page-title">Devices</h2>

<p class="hint">
    Set up each device in the Overland iOS app's settings with these 3 fields:
</p>
<ul class="hint-list">
    <li>
        <strong>Receiver URL</strong> -- the same for every device, no per-device parts:<br>
        <code id="overland-receiver-url">{{ $overland_base_url | e }}</code>
        <button type="button" class="icon-btn copy-value-btn" data-copy-value="{{ $overland_base_url | e }}" title="Copy Receiver URL"><i class="bx bx-copy"></i></button>
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Access Token</strong> -- that device's own <strong>device_key</strong> from the table
        below (Overland sends this back as the request's actual authentication).
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Device ID</strong> (optional) -- that device's own <strong>guid</strong> from the
        table below, purely so it's easy to recognize which device a point came from later; not
        needed for authentication, since Access Token alone already identifies the device.
    </li>
</ul>
<p class="hint">
    Click the <i class="bx bx-copy"></i> button next to a guid/device_key value below to copy just
    that value.
</p>

<div class="settings-table-scroll">{{ $devices_table }}</div>

<hr>

<h3>Add a device</h3>
{{ $devices_form }}

<script src="{{rel_url('js/devices.js')}}"></script>
